<rml>
<head>
	<title>shader decorator</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="/folio/folio.rcss"/>
	<style>
		/*
			decorator: shader("...") - the effects RCSS has no syntax for.

			RmlUi passes the string through untouched, which is where a backend would run a
			fragment shader of its own. Slate has no seam for that, and none of these needs one:
			each is a pure function of position over the element's box, so it is evaluated once
			into a small texture. Both renderers therefore draw the same picture from the same
			code, which a pair of hand-written shaders would not.

			additive and sweep write zero alpha. RmlUi composites premultiplied - src + dst * (1-a)
			- so a colour with no alpha adds to what is under it. No blend state to change, and
			that is the whole reason additive was said to be out of reach.

			Note the order: the shader is listed FIRST and the gradient second. Comma separated
			decorators paint in reverse source order, so the first named ends up on top, exactly
			as CSS background-image layers do. Listed the other way round the gradient covers the
			effect and nothing appears to happen.
		*/
		body
		{
			font-family: Inter;
			font-size: 14dp;
			color: #e8e8f0;
			background-color: #0d0d12;
			padding: 20dp;
			width: 100%;
			height: 100%;
			box-sizing: border-box;
		}

		.label { font-size: 12dp; color: #8a8a99; margin-bottom: 4dp; }
		.row { margin-bottom: 16dp; }

		/* Something with detail underneath, so an additive pass is unmistakable. */
		.plate
		{
			height: 90dp;
			border-radius: 8dp;
			decorator: linear-gradient(90deg, #24405e, #6f3b52);
		}

		.flash   { decorator: shader("additive #ff5028c0"), linear-gradient(90deg, #24405e, #6f3b52); }
		.crt     { decorator: shader("scanlines #7fe8ff90 0.16 0.5"), linear-gradient(90deg, #24405e, #6f3b52); }
		.sheen   { decorator: shader("sweep #ffffffb0 0.35 0.3 15"), linear-gradient(90deg, #24405e, #6f3b52); }
		.cooling { decorator: shader("sweep #40ffa0ff 0.7 0.5 90"), linear-gradient(90deg, #24405e, #6f3b52); }
	</style>
</head>
<body>
	<div class="label">no shader</div>
	<div class="row plate"></div>

	<div class="label">shader("additive #ff5028c0") - a hit flash</div>
	<div class="row plate flash"></div>

	<div class="label">shader("scanlines #7fe8ff90 0.16 0.5")</div>
	<div class="row plate crt"></div>

	<div class="label">shader("sweep #ffffffb0 0.35 0.3 15") - sheen</div>
	<div class="row plate sheen"></div>

	<div class="label">shader("sweep #40ffa0ff 0.7 0.5 90") - a vertical band</div>
	<div class="row plate cooling"></div>
</body>
</rml>
